  "instructions": [
    {
      "primary_message": "This recipe makes about 8 (1-cup) servings of beef bulgogi.\n\n",
      "secondary_message": null
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Wash and dry the fresh produce.\n\n",
      "secondary_message": "1 mango\n4 (1 inch) piece ginger root"
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Peel mango and slice flesh away from the pit, starting with the flat sides; roughly chop the flesh. Place in a blender.\n\n",
      "secondary_message": null
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Juice limes into the blender.\n\n",
      "secondary_message": null
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Peel and roughly chop ginger and garlic. Add both to the blender along with soy sauce, sugar, gocuhujang, vinegar, salt, and pepper. Blend on high until the marinade is smooth, scraping down the sides of the blender as needed. Transfer to a large bowl.\n\n",
      "secondary_message": "6 clove garlic\n⅓ cup soy sauce\n¼ cup brown sugar\n3 tbsp gochujang\n2 tbsp rice vinegar\n1 tsp salt\n½ tsp black pepper"
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Pat steak dry with paper towels, then slice crosswise into thin strips. Add to the bowl with the marinade, stir to coat, and set aside for 1 hour.\n\n",
      "secondary_message": null
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "When the steak is done marinating, preheat a large skillet over medium-high heat.\n\n",
      "secondary_message": null
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Once the skillet is hot, add oil and swirl to coat the bottom. Working in batches, add steak (leaving any excess marinade in the bowl) and stir-fry until cooked through, 4-5 minutes. Transfer to a large baking sheet pan, spread out in an even layer, and set aside to cool, 15 minutes.\n\n",
      "secondary_message": "2 tbsp toasted sesame oil"
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "STORING: When the beef has cooled, divide between resealable plastic bags, pressing out as much air as possible. Place in the freezer and store for up to 2 months. HEATING: For best results, thaw steak in the fridge overnight. Stir-fry in a hot skillet until heated through, 3-4 minutes. Use as a base for stir-fries, rice bowls, or even tacos!",
      "secondary_message": null
    }
  ],
